  - type: metin
    metin: Access to psychological services in North Cyprus is a developing area compared with larger cities in Turkey and Europe. In recent years, however, the number of private psychology centres has grown significantly, and online sessions have largely removed geographical barriers. Being informed makes it far easier to find the right support.
  - type: metin
    baslik: How does psychology work in North Cyprus?
    metin: |-
      Psychological support in TRNC is available through two main channels: the psychiatry clinics of state hospitals, and private psychology centres. The state channel focuses primarily on psychiatric assessment and medication management, while private psychology centres offer a more suitable environment for talk therapy, behavioural and cognitive interventions, and longer-term psychological work.

      In a private psychology centre the process typically works as follows: [the first session](/en/blog/before-starting-therapy.html) is an assessment where the psychologist gets to know you and your reasons for coming; together you then set goals; and regular weekly or fortnightly sessions follow from there.
  - type: ozel
    html: |-
      <div>
                  <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">The difference between a psychologist and a psychiatrist</h2>
                  <div class="space-y-3">
                    <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                      <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Psychologist</h3>
                      <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">A psychologist has a degree and postgraduate qualification in psychology and provides talk therapy. They cannot prescribe medication. Psychologists work with a wide range of issues including anxiety, depression, relationship problems, trauma, grief and anger.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-5 border border-warm-tertiary">
                      <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-1.5">Psychiatrist</h3>
                      <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">A psychiatrist is a medical doctor who has specialised in psychiatry. They can prescribe medication and are involved in the diagnosis and treatment of serious psychiatric conditions. In some cases a psychologist and psychiatrist work together.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-4 text-sm">For most people — anxiety, stress, relationship difficulties, low mood — starting with a psychologist is sufficient. If a psychiatric assessment is needed, your psychologist will refer you.</p>
                </div>
